1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,400
Cortisol belly and cortisol face are all over your feed right now — before you buy a "cortisol detox" supplement, here's what endocrinologists actually say.

2
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:22,720
Cortisol dysregulation can contribute to abdominal fat storage — that part is real, since visceral fat carries an unusually high density of cortisol-activating receptors.

3
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:32,160
But "cortisol face" isn't a recognized diagnosis, and cortisol alone rarely explains the overnight bloating some creators claim.

4
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:47,040
Three everyday habits do measurably raise cortisol: hard workouts without recovery days, wildly inconsistent sleep schedules, and chasing trendy fixes instead of techniques with real evidence behind them.

5
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:52,240
First is stacking high-intensity workouts without recovery days.

6
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:57,600
Exercise is supposed to raise cortisol briefly, then let it drop as you recover.

7
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:07,360
Studies on endurance and resistance training show that repeating hard sessions without enough rest keeps resting cortisol elevated for weeks.

8
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:15,120
Build in at least one lower-intensity recovery day between hard sessions instead of pushing through every day.

9
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:19,760
Second is a sleep schedule that shifts wildly from day to day.

10
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:28,480
Cortisol follows a daily rhythm — it spikes about thirty to forty-five minutes after you wake up, then tapers off by night.

11
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:38,800
Going to bed and waking up at different times each day disrupts that rhythm, so cortisol stays higher into the evening instead of winding down.

12
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:45,520
Getting enough total sleep matters, and so does a consistent wake time — even on weekends.

13
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:55,280
Third is chasing whatever's trending — cold plunges, detox teas — instead of stress techniques that actually have trial data behind them.

14
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:06,320
Mindfulness-based programs have been shown in randomized trials to measurably lower cortisol, while cold plunges and detox teas don't have that evidence.

15
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:13,040
A short daily practice like guided breathing is a better use of your time than a supplement stack.

16
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:25,360
Spacing out hard workouts, keeping a consistent wake time, and picking stress techniques backed by real trials will do more for your cortisol than any thirty-day cleanse.

17
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:39,040
If you're seeing rapid weight gain along with muscle weakness or new purple stretch marks, that combination points to Cushing's syndrome, not everyday stress — worth getting an actual test from a doctor.
